Thank you for your interest in the Master of Natural Science (MNS) program at Arizona State University. The MNS program is a summer graduate program for in-service high school science teachers who desire professional training rather than research training. The program is 30 units designed to be completed in 3 summers.

The foundation of the MNS program is Modeling Instruction, extending and deepening the Modeling Instruction program with eight courses in integrated science and contemporary physics. 

For more information on the MNS program and how to apply, please visit https://physics.asu.edu/admissions/mns-admissions. If you have any additional questions, please let us know.


